    "created_at": "2017-03-16T21:44:04Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-03-16T21:47:15Z",
    "body": "I have confirmed that Safari Tech Preview has not updated to follow the (current) spec yet, at least for `createElementNS(\"a\", \"a:0\")`, so I think this is landable with a clear conscience.\r\n\r\nI also searched bugs.webkit.org for createElementNS, NamespaceError, InvalidCharacterError, NAMESPACE_ERR, and INVALID_CHARACTER_ERR with no results that indicate they're tracking this.\r\n\r\nOh, and I tested Edge and it also does InvalidCharacterError.",
